# Lines of code

https://github.com/ronin-chain/katana-operation-contracts/blob/27f9d28e00958bf3494fa405a8a5acdcd5ecdc5d/src/aggregate-router/modules/katana/v3/V3SwapRouter.sol#L143
https://github.com/ronin-chain/katana-operation-contracts/blob/27f9d28e00958bf3494fa405a8a5acdcd5ecdc5d/src/aggregate-router/base/Dispatcher.sol#L51
https://github.com/ronin-chain/katana-operation-contracts/blob/27f9d28e00958bf3494fa405a8a5acdcd5ecdc5d/src/aggregate-router/modules/katana/v3/V3SwapRouter.sol#L93
https://github.com/ronin-chain/katana-operation-contracts/blob/27f9d28e00958bf3494fa405a8a5acdcd5ecdc5d/src/aggregate-router/libraries/Constants.sol#L36
https://github.com/ronin-chain/katana-operation-contracts/blob/27f9d28e00958bf3494fa405a8a5acdcd5ecdc5d/src/aggregate-router/modules/katana/v3/V3Path.sol#L14
https://github.com/ronin-chain/katana-operation-contracts/blob/27f9d28e00958bf3494fa405a8a5acdcd5ecdc5d/src/aggregate-router/modules/katana/v3/V3SwapRouter.sol#L48


# Vulnerability details

# Proof of concept

The code add [more authorization](https://github.com/ronin-chain/katana-operation-contracts/blob/27f9d28e00958bf3494fa405a8a5acdcd5ecdc5d/src/aggregate-router/modules/katana/v3/V3SwapRouter.sol#L143) based on the uniswap v3 code in V3SwapRouter.sol

```solidity
  function checkAuthorizedV3Path(bytes calldata path) internal view { // @audit this must have bugs
    uint256 length = path.length / Constants.NEXT_V3_POOL_OFFSET + 1;
    address[] memory tokens = new address[](length);
    for (uint256 i; i < length; ++i) {
      tokens[i] = path.decodeFirstToken();
      if (i + 1 < length) path = path.skipToken();
    }
    if (!IKatanaGovernance(KATANA_GOVERNANCE).isAuthorized(tokens, msg.sender)) revert V3UnauthorizedSwap();
  }
```

this is used for path validation in [Dispatcher code](https://github.com/ronin-chain/katana-operation-contracts/blob/27f9d28e00958bf3494fa405a8a5acdcd5ecdc5d/src/aggregate-router/base/Dispatcher.sol#L51)

```solidity
bytes calldata path = inputs.toBytes(3);
    address payer = payerIsUser ? lockedBy : address(this);
    v3SwapExactInput(map(recipient), amountIn, amountOutMin, path, payer);
    checkAuthorizedV3Path(path); // place the check here to avoid stack too deep error
}
```

However, the checkAuthorizedV3Path fails to correctly get how many token involved.

A reference implementation can be [V3SwapRouter.sol#v3SwapExactInput](https://github.com/ronin-chain/katana-operation-contracts/blob/27f9d28e00958bf3494fa405a8a5acdcd5ecdc5d/src/aggregate-router/modules/katana/v3/V3SwapRouter.sol#L93)

```solidity
  function v3SwapExactInput(
    address recipient,
    uint256 amountIn,
    uint256 amountOutMinimum,
    bytes calldata path,
    address payer
  ) internal {
    // use amountIn == Constants.CONTRACT_BALANCE as a flag to swap the entire balance of the contract
    if (amountIn == Constants.CONTRACT_BALANCE) {
      address tokenIn = path.decodeFirstToken();
      amountIn = ERC20(tokenIn).balanceOf(address(this));
    }

    uint256 amountOut;
    while (true) {
      bool hasMultiplePools = path.hasMultiplePools(); // <=====

      // the outputs of prior swaps become the inputs to subsequent ones
      (int256 amount0Delta, int256 amount1Delta, bool zeroForOne) = _swap(
        amountIn.toInt256(),
        hasMultiplePools ? address(this) : recipient, // for intermediate swaps, this contract custodies
        path.getFirstPool(), // only the first pool is needed
        payer, // for intermediate swaps, this contract custodies
        true
      );

      amountIn = uint256(-(zeroForOne ? amount1Delta : amount0Delta));

      // decide whether to continue or terminate
      if (hasMultiplePools) {
        payer = address(this); 
        path = path.skipToken(); // <====
      } else {
        amountOut = amountIn;
        break;
      }
    }

```

as we can see, only when the path hasMultiplePools is true, we skip token and capture a new path.

to understand path.hasMultiplePools() and path.skipToken(), we need to reference other code.

the [constants.sol code](https://github.com/ronin-chain/katana-operation-contracts/blob/27f9d28e00958bf3494fa405a8a5acdcd5ecdc5d/src/aggregate-router/libraries/Constants.sol#L36) shows the length of MULTIPLE_V3_POOLS_MIN_LENGTH and NEXT_V3_POOL_OFFSET and V3_POP_OFFSET 

```solidity
  /// @dev The length of the bytes encoded address
  uint256 internal constant ADDR_SIZE = 20;

  /// @dev The length of the bytes encoded fee
  uint256 internal constant V3_FEE_SIZE = 3;

  /// @dev The offset of a single token address (20) and pool fee (3)
  uint256 internal constant NEXT_V3_POOL_OFFSET = ADDR_SIZE + V3_FEE_SIZE;

  /// @dev The offset of an encoded pool key
  /// Token (20) + Fee (3) + Token (20) = 43
  uint256 internal constant V3_POP_OFFSET = NEXT_V3_POOL_OFFSET + ADDR_SIZE;

  /// @dev The minimum length of an encoding that contains 2 or more pools
  uint256 internal constant MULTIPLE_V3_POOLS_MIN_LENGTH = V3_POP_OFFSET + NEXT_V3_POOL_OFFSET;
```

and we have the [helper functions](https://github.com/ronin-chain/katana-operation-contracts/blob/27f9d28e00958bf3494fa405a8a5acdcd5ecdc5d/src/aggregate-router/modules/katana/v3/V3Path.sol#L14)

```solidity
library V3Path {
  using BytesLib for bytes;

  /// @notice Returns true iff the path contains two or more pools
  /// @param path The encoded swap path
  /// @return True if path contains two or more pools, otherwise false
  function hasMultiplePools(bytes calldata path) internal pure returns (bool) {
    return path.length >= Constants.MULTIPLE_V3_POOLS_MIN_LENGTH;
  }

  /// @notice Decodes the first pool in path
  /// @param path The bytes encoded swap path
  /// @return tokenA The first token of the given pool
  /// @return fee The fee level of the pool
  /// @return tokenB The second token of the given pool
  function decodeFirstPool(bytes calldata path) internal pure returns (address, uint24, address) {
    return path.toPool();
  }

  /// @notice Gets the segment corresponding to the first pool in the path
  /// @param path The bytes encoded swap path
  /// @return The segment containing all data necessary to target the first pool in the path
  function getFirstPool(bytes calldata path) internal pure returns (bytes calldata) {
    return path[:Constants.V3_POP_OFFSET];
  }

  function decodeFirstToken(bytes calldata path) internal pure returns (address tokenA) {
    tokenA = path.toAddress();
  }

  /// @notice Skips a token + fee element
  /// @param path The swap path
  function skipToken(bytes calldata path) internal pure returns (bytes calldata) {
    return path[Constants.NEXT_V3_POOL_OFFSET:];
  }
}
```

now we take a look at the [new code](https://github.com/ronin-chain/katana-operation-contracts/blob/27f9d28e00958bf3494fa405a8a5acdcd5ecdc5d/src/aggregate-router/modules/katana/v3/V3SwapRouter.sol#L143) again

```solidity
  function checkAuthorizedV3Path(bytes calldata path) internal view { // @audit this must have bugs
    uint256 length = path.length / Constants.NEXT_V3_POOL_OFFSET + 1;
    address[] memory tokens = new address[](length);
    for (uint256 i; i < length; ++i) {
      tokens[i] = path.decodeFirstToken();
      if (i + 1 < length) path = path.skipToken();
    }
    if (!IKatanaGovernance(KATANA_GOVERNANCE).isAuthorized(tokens, msg.sender)) revert V3UnauthorizedSwap();
  }
```

the length is computed from  path.length / Constants.NEXT_V3_POOL_OFFSET + 1, and Constants.NEXT_V3_POOL_OFFSET is 23 bytes

however, as we can see, the encoded pool key is V3_POP_OFFSET = 
 Token (20) + Fee (3) + Token (20) = 43 bytes,

then using path.length / Constants.NEXT_V3_POOL_OFFSET + 1 cannot truly get how many token is involved

the code below get both tokenIn and tokenOut, while path.decodeFirstToken() only get the tokenIn and missing the the token out.

```solidity
   // because exact output swaps are executed in reverse order, in this case tokenOut is actually tokenIn
   (address tokenIn, uint24 fee, address tokenOut) = path.decodeFirstPool();
```

# Recommendation

A good reference is [V3SwapRouter.sol#katanaV3SwapCallback](https://github.com/ronin-chain/katana-operation-contracts/blob/27f9d28e00958bf3494fa405a8a5acdcd5ecdc5d/src/aggregate-router/modules/katana/v3/V3SwapRouter.sol#L48)

```solidity
  function katanaV3SwapCallback(int256 amount0Delta, int256 amount1Delta, bytes calldata data) external {
    if (amount0Delta <= 0 && amount1Delta <= 0) revert V3InvalidSwap(); // swaps entirely within 0-liquidity regions are not supported
    (, address payer) = abi.decode(data, (bytes, address));
    bytes calldata path = data.toBytes(0);

    // because exact output swaps are executed in reverse order, in this case tokenOut is actually tokenIn
   (address tokenIn, uint24 fee, address tokenOut) = path.decodeFirstPool();

    if (computePoolAddress(tokenIn, tokenOut, fee) != msg.sender) revert V3InvalidCaller();

    (bool isExactInput, uint256 amountToPay) =
      amount0Delta > 0 ? (tokenIn < tokenOut, uint256(amount0Delta)) : (tokenOut < tokenIn, uint256(amount1Delta));

    if (isExactInput) {
      // Pay the pool (msg.sender)
      payOrPermit2Transfer(tokenIn, payer, msg.sender, amountToPay);
    } else {
      // either initiate the next swap or pay
      if (path.hasMultiplePools()) {
        // this is an intermediate step so the payer is actually this contract
        path = path.skipToken();
        _swap(-amountToPay.toInt256(), msg.sender, path, payer, false);
      } else {
        if (amountToPay > maxAmountInCached) revert V3TooMuchRequested();
        // note that because exact output swaps are executed in reverse order, tokenOut is actually tokenIn
        payOrPermit2Transfer(tokenOut, payer, msg.sender, amountToPay);
      }
    }
  }
```

the path.decodeFirstPool can get all tokenIn and tokenOut involved, the code can store them in an array.

then the code should check if the path.hasMultiplePools is true, then skip token.

in this way, the checkAuthorizedV3Path can get all token involved.


## Assessed type

en/de-code

# Lines of code

https://github.com/ronin-chain/katana-v3-contracts/blob/03c80179e04f40d96f06c451ea494bb18f2a58fc/src/periphery/NonfungiblePositionManager.sol#L246


# Vulnerability details

## Description

A critical access control vulnerability was discovered in the `NonfungiblePositionManager` contract within the Katana V3 protocol. The vulnerability lies in the `increaseLiquidity` function, which allows any address to increase the liquidity of a position, regardless of whether they own the position or not.

This function fails to verify if the caller has the appropriate permissions to modify the liquidity of the position associated with the provided `tokenId`. This oversight enables unauthorized users to increase liquidity on any position without ownership or approval. This behavior is highly problematic as it violates the expected permission boundaries, allowing an attacker to manipulate user positions arbitrarily.

## Vulnerability Details

- **Contract**: `NonfungiblePositionManager`
- **Function**: `increaseLiquidity`
- **Vulnerability Type**: Access Control Violation
- **Severity**: High

## Proof of Concept

The following test demonstrates the vulnerability: (in KatanaV3Pool.t.sol)

1. Define an unauthorized user and position token ID:
    ```solidity
    address unauthorized = makeAddr("unauthorized");
    uint positionTokenId;
    ```

2. Mint tokens to the unauthorized user for testing purposes in the setUp:
    ```solidity
    ERC20Mock(token0).mint(address(unauthorized), 100e18);
    ERC20Mock(token1).mint(address(unauthorized), 100e18);
    ```

3. Implement the test function to simulate unauthorized liquidity increase:
    ```solidity
    function test_unauthorizedIncreaseLiquidity() public {
        // Get initial liquidity
        (, , , , , , , uint128 initialLiquidity, , , , ) = positionManager.positions(positionTokenId);
        emit log_named_uint("Initial liquidity:", initialLiquidity);

        // Switch to unauthorized user
        vm.startPrank(unauthorized);

        // Approve tokens for unauthorized user
        ERC20Mock(token0).approve(address(positionManager), type(uint256).max);
        ERC20Mock(token1).approve(address(positionManager), type(uint256).max);

        // Attempt to increase liquidity as unauthorized user
        INonfungiblePositionManager.IncreaseLiquidityParams memory params = INonfungiblePositionManager.IncreaseLiquidityParams({
            tokenId: positionTokenId,
            amount0Desired: 1e17,
            amount1Desired: 1e17,
            amount0Min: 0,
            amount1Min: 0,
            deadline: block.timestamp + 1
        });

        // If proper access control is missing, this succeeds
        (uint128 addedLiquidity, uint256 amount0, uint256 amount1) = positionManager.increaseLiquidity(params);
        console.log("Unauthorized liquidity increase succeeded");
        emit log_named_uint("Added liquidity:", addedLiquidity);
        emit log_named_uint("Added amount0:", amount0);
        emit log_named_uint("Added amount1:", amount1);

        vm.stopPrank();

        // Check final liquidity
        (, , , , , , , uint128 finalLiquidity, , , , ) = positionManager.positions(positionTokenId);
        emit log_named_uint("Final liquidity:", finalLiquidity);

        // Validate the liquidity increase
        assertEq(uint256(finalLiquidity), uint256(initialLiquidity) + uint256(addedLiquidity), "Liquidity should have increased by the added amount");

        // Calculate and log the percentage increase
        uint256 percentageIncrease = (uint256(addedLiquidity) * 100) / uint256(initialLiquidity);
        emit log_named_uint("Percentage increase in liquidity:", percentageIncrease);
    }
    ```

4. Run the test:
    ```bash
    forge test --match-test test_unauthorizedIncreaseLiquidity -vvv
    ```

**Test Output**:

```bash
Initial liquidity:: 802053
Unauthorized liquidity increase succeeded
Added liquidity:: 80205384747467308
Added amount0:: 9958462078330347
Added amount1:: 100000000000000000
Final liquidity:: 80205384748269361
Percentage increase in liquidity:: 10000010566317
```

This proves that unauthorized users can successfully increase liquidity without permission, leading to potential misuse of liquidity positions.

## Recommended Fix

To prevent this vulnerability, implement proper access control in the `increaseLiquidity` function:

1. Create an `isAuthorizedForToken` modifier:

    ```solidity
    modifier isAuthorizedForToken(uint256 tokenId) {
        require(msg.sender == ownerOf(tokenId) || isApprovedForAll(ownerOf(tokenId), msg.sender), "Not authorized");
        _;
    }
    ```

2. Apply the modifier to the `increaseLiquidity` function:

    ```solidity
    function increaseLiquidity(IncreaseLiquidityParams calldata params)
        external
        payable
        override
        isAuthorizedForToken(params.tokenId)  // Add this modifier
        checkDeadline(params.deadline)
        returns (uint128 liquidity, uint256 amount0, uint256 amount1)
    {
        // Existing function body
    }
    ```


## Assessed type

Access Control

# Lines of code

https://github.com/ronin-chain/katana-v3-contracts/blob/03c80179e04f40d96f06c451ea494bb18f2a58fc/src/core/KatanaV3Pool.sol#L111-L114
https://github.com/ronin-chain/katana-v3-contracts/blob/03c80179e04f40d96f06c451ea494bb18f2a58fc/src/core/KatanaV3Pool.sol#L117-L131


# Vulnerability details

## Proof of Concept
In the `KatanaV3Pool::constructor`, the factory variable is initialised with address(1). 

```
  constructor() {
    // disable immutables initialization
    factory = address(1);
  }
```
At this point the state variables are not yet initialized. 

example: The below two state variables are not yet initialized. 

```
 address public override governance;
 address public override positionManager;

```

But, these variables are initialized via `initializeImmutables` function as below.

```
 function initializeImmutables(address factory_, address token0_, address token1_, uint24 fee_, int24 tickSpacing_)
    public
    virtual
    override
  {
    require(factory == address(0), "AII");

    (factory, token0, token1, fee, tickSpacing) = (factory_, token0_, token1_, fee_, tickSpacing_);

    // cache these immutable addresses for gas savings when swaps, mints, or burns are performed
==>    governance = IKatanaV3Factory(factory_).owner();
==>    positionManager = IKatanaGovernance(governance).getPositionManager();

    maxLiquidityPerTick = Tick.tickSpacingToMaxLiquidityPerTick(tickSpacing_);
  }
```

But, the initialise function is disabled because of the require validation in the function that expects the factory address to be address(0), while the factory was assigned adddress(1) in the constructor,

As as result the `initializeImmutables` function will not work as expected and would revert.

## Recommended Mitigation Steps

In the constructor, initialise the factory as zero address.
 factory = address(0);


